nodes.body:
@sohom-cs Thanks again for the detailed earlier review. I’ve addressed the cancellation/liveness concerns in the current revision.

The main changes are:

* expired rounds now actively request cancellation instead of releasing inflight transfers;
* pins remain held until the transport confirms a terminal/cancelled state;
* cancellation is retried while transfers remain inflight;
* abort interaction, late completion/failure, and never-completing-transfer cases now have regression coverage.

Full tiering validation on the current revision: 439 passed, 1 skipped.

Could you take another look when you have a chance, especially at the cancellation-pending / pin-lifetime behavior? Happy to address anything remaining. Thanks!

